      "docs.g3.cta": "Open the demo →",
      "docs.s2": "The signals CSV file",
      "docs.s2p": "It's the only point of contact between BetRelay and your software: BetRelay writes a row, the software reads it and decides whether to bet. These are the 14 columns BetRelay produces, in the order they appear in the file.",
      "docs.csv1.tag": "Format", "docs.csv1.h": "📄 How the file is built",
      "docs.csv1.p": "Column names on the first line, all values between double quotes, UTF-8 with BOM. One active row at a time: after the timeout the file goes back to header only.",
      "docs.csv2.tag": "Recognition", "docs.csv2.h": "🎯 By id or by names",
      "docs.csv2.p": "The software can identify the selection from the Betfair ids (<code>MarketId</code> + <code>SelectionId</code>) or from the names (<code>EventName</code> + <code>MarketType</code> + <code>SelectionName</code>). With the name method, the source language must match the one the software uses to read the catalogue.",
